title: The Left Breaks Away
subtitle: Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow will not accept Levi's party.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month >= 9 and crisis = 0 and e21_left_split_pending = 1 and left_split = 0 and offensive_gone = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 9
on-arrival: e21_left_split_pending = 0

= The Left Breaks Away

Since Jena the Berlin district has refused to distribute the Rote Fahne's articles on the united front. In September Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow call a conference of the opposition. Berlin comes, and parts of Hamburg, the Ruhr and the Palatinate. They say the party has become a second USPD under Levi, and that the revolutionaries must save the International's honour in Germany, alone if need be.

The KAPD has already offered them a home. Zinoviev has not yet decided whose side he is on.

- @let_go: Let them go.
- @leaders: Expel Fischer and Maslow, and keep their members.
- @offer: Make a last offer: seats in the Zentrale.

@let_go
subtitle: The party loses the Left, and its districts, but the line is clear.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_split = 1;
Q.offensive_gone = 1;
Q.e21_left_lost = 0;
var heir = (Q.leading_faction == 'offensive') ? 'unionist' : Q.leading_faction;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] == 'offensive') {
        var lost = Q['district_' + d + '_members'] * 0.5;
        Q.e21_left_lost += lost;
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] -= lost;
        Q['district_' + d + '_faction'] = heir;
        Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = 50;
    }
}
Q.e21_left_lost = Math.round(Q.e21_left_lost);
Q.offensive_satisfaction = 0;
if (Q.junior_faction == 'offensive') {
    Q.junior_faction = 0;
}
Q.kapd_exists = 1;
Q.kapd_relation -= 10;
Q.unity += 12;
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6;
!}

The opposition walks out and founds the Communist Left. Within weeks it is talking about fusion with the KAPD. About [+ e21_left_lost +] thousand members follow it. The party that remains is smaller, calmer and, for the first time, of one mind.

@leaders
subtitle: The Right's way: cut off the head. A smaller split, and a bitter one.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_split = 1;
Q.district_berlin_members *= 0.8;
Q.district_berlin_loyalty -= 10;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 20;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.unity -= 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

The Zentrale expels Fischer, Maslow and a dozen of their lieutenants. Part of Berlin goes with them. Most of the Left's members stay in the party, and they do not forget.

@offer
subtitle: No split. The Left joins the Zentrale, and Levi's line is watered down.
on-arrival: {!
Q.junior_faction = 'offensive';
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 20;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.unity += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

At the last moment the Zentrale offers the opposition three seats and a promise that the united front will be applied "from below". Fischer accepts, and tells her friends that it is only a truce.
